# Combined CPU-bottleneck candidate: decode metadata fast-path patch +
# async scheduling, both attacking the same hypothesis from different
# angles.
#
# Why this candidate: across 4 official H200 submissions (baseline,
# v0.25.1, and two ShortConv-quantization variants -- see
# SUBMISSION_RESULTS.md "VERDICT (2026-07-25)"), TBT median was 4ms in
# EVERY run, completely unchanged despite quantizing an additional ~168M
# previously-unquantized parameters. That rules out GPU compute/weight-
# bandwidth as the real H200/MIG decode bottleneck. The likely culprit:
# vLLM V1 runs 3 separate processes (API server, EngineCore, GPU worker)
# competing for what is likely a small vCPU allocation on the MIG slice --
# CPU-side per-step overhead (metadata upload, IPC, scheduling, SSE
# serialization), not GPU work, is probably the real floor.
#
# This image stacks two mitigations for that:
# - patches/apply_vllm_decode_metadata_fastpath.py: avoids re-uploading
#   req_indices/query_pos/num_scheduled_tokens and the discard_request_mask
#   every step for pure one-token decode batches. Measured only +1.4% TBT
#   locally (RTX 3090/Blackwell, no real CPU constraint there) -- but that
#   number was measured where CPU was never the bottleneck, so it likely
#   understates the real H200 value.
# - --async-scheduling (added in the compose command, not baked into this
#   image): overlaps CPU scheduling work with GPU execution. KNOWN RISK:
#   a prior local probe on this same flag found 2/420 gibberish outputs
#   (EXPERIMENTS.md "Async scheduling probe", session 10) -- re-verify
#   output coherence before trusting any ERS improvement from this image.
#
# Base is v0.22.1 (matches the fp8-v1 image behind the 60.89 baseline) --
# NOT v0.25.1, after the confirmed v0.25.1 interaction hazard with the
# ShortConv patch (unrelated code path, but no reason to reintroduce an
# unnecessary variable here).
#
# Build context must be the repository root:
#   docker build -f submission/Dockerfile.fp8-metadata-fastpath-async-local -t <image>:<tag> .
#
# Before building, copy/sync the official BF16 checkpoint into:
#   submission/model/
FROM vllm/vllm-openai:v0.22.1

RUN pip install --no-cache-dir xxhash

COPY patches/apply_vllm_decode_metadata_fastpath.py /tmp/apply_vllm_decode_metadata_fastpath.py
RUN python3 /tmp/apply_vllm_decode_metadata_fastpath.py && rm /tmp/apply_vllm_decode_metadata_fastpath.py

COPY submission/model /model

ENV HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 \
    TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1 \
    VLLM_NO_USAGE_STATS=1 \
    DO_NOT_TRACK=1

EXPOSE 8000
